    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (routing table: operating company, cyclical US industrial). CSX is a Class I freight railroad (~20,000 route miles, eastern US) -- a capital-intensive quasi-infrastructure operator whose value is its free cash flow after maintenance/growth capex; none of the non-FCF rows apply. Adaptations applied: cyclical (risk charged once, in flows/weights), lease treatment stated. FY0 = FY2025 (revenue $14,092M, EBITDA $6,201M = 44.0%, depressed by Hurricane Helene Blue Ridge rebuild, Howard Street Tunnel detours, weak coal/merchandise pricing and Q3-Q4 2025 restructuring). FY2025 reported FCF $1,711M is a TROUGH: capex $2,902M (20.6% of revenue) was elevated by the Blue Ridge and Howard Street projects; TTM to Q2 2026 capex is $2,526M (17.4%) and H1-2026 $1,119M (15.1%). last_fcf ($1,657M) is recorded for audit only -- the forward flows are built from components on unlevered EBIT and do not carry the FY2025 margin forward. H1-2026 EBITDA margin 48.3% (Q2 48.7%) reflects the post-Sept-2025 cost programme under the new CEO. Buybacks funded (repurchaser), so the flat count is paid for in cash. Analysis JSON was not yet available at build time; narratives drawn from filings data and business knowledge.",
